body:
Two root causes drove ~50s load times: a duplicate `run()` call in `init()` fired two full API round-trips on every page load, and `safeFetchList()` had no client-side caching so each reload re-hit the backend. No email alerting existed for expiring or understocked products.

## Frontend (`index.html`)

- **Remove duplicate `run()` call** — `init()` called `run()` inside `if(sups.length>0)` _and_ unconditionally at the end; the first call is removed so one API request fires instead of two
- **`sessionStorage` cache for `safeFetchList()`** — 5-min TTL; reloads within the same session skip the `?list=true` backend round-trip entirely

```js
// Before: run() called twice
if (sups.length > 0) { termInp.value = sups[0]; await run(); } // ← removed
// ...
await run(); // ← kept

// safeFetchList: now checks sessionStorage before fetching
const LIST_CACHE_TTL_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;
const cached = sessionStorage.getItem('listCache');
if (cached) { const { t, data } = JSON.parse(cached); if (Date.now() - t < LIST_CACHE_TTL_MS) return data; }
```

## Backend patches (`backend/optimizaciones_backend.gs`)

Drop-in wrappers and helpers to copy into the Apps Script editor:

- **F8 read wrappers with `CacheService`** — `getRecepcionYTransitoMap_DesdeF8_Cached()`, `getReservasMap_DesdeF8_Cached()`, `getForecastMensualMap_DesdeUE_Cached()` cache each external spreadsheet read (2–8 s each) for 5 min; replace the 3 direct calls in `doGet()` and `updateCoverageReport()`
- **`doGet_list_optimizado_()`** — reads the pre-built `Index` sheet instead of scanning all of `Data` for the `?list=true` response
- **`buildServerCacheKey_()`** — builds the server cache key from an ordered array, explicitly excluding `ts` so browser cache-busting doesn't invalidate the server cache

## Email alerts (`backend/alertas_correo.gs`)

New GAS file implementing a consolidated daily alert email:

- Reads `Reporte_Vencimientos` and `Reporte_Abastecimiento` sheets
- Classifies rows into levels: 🔴 VENCIDO/AGOTADO · 🟠 CRÍTICO · 🟡 RIESGO · 🟢 ALERTA/BAJO
- All thresholds centralized in `ALERT_CONFIG` (days to expiry, months of coverage, recipients, min send level)
- Single HTML email with tables sorted by priority; one email per run regardless of product count
- `testEnviarAlertas()` for manual verification; `configurarTriggerDiario()` / `eliminarTriggerAlertas()` for trigger lifecycle

